Ryujinx AST optimizer: keep atomics, calls and image atomics whose result is unused as statements (Maxwell RED,
ATOM with an RZ destination), and keep call arguments in variables (SPIR-V passes them by pointer).
From MacNativeGames (games/totk/tools/totk_xlate/patches, MIT), which found that Tears of the Kingdom's
sun-visibility reduction kernel lost its atomicMin without them. Applied at build time by
translator/Ryujinx.Graphics.Shader.csproj to a copy in private/build; the checkout in private/third_party stays
untouched. The Ryujinx code in the context lines is MIT.

--- a/src/Ryujinx.Graphics.Shader/StructuredIr/AstOptimizer.cs	2026-07-17 15:57:07.000000000 +0300
